From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:21:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: Revert "ACPICA: avoid accessing operands
 out-of-bounds"

This reverts commit 77ab44ba5937.

This patch was retired from the stonking linux 7.2 kernel by its owner
and recorded as obsolete in Changes.md ("UBUNTU: Changes.md: Drop more
obsolete sauce", f3f1bdc6d342 on stonking master-next). Drop it here as
well, so that 7.3 linux does not bring back a patch 7.2 no longer carries.

Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00252
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@f00fd8012094a771a39b84484ba16e0c18f6b93b
---
 drivers/acpi/acpica/dswexec.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/acpica/dswexec.c b/drivers/acpi/acpica/dswexec.c
index a89ddd1ab48c..675aaa671012 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/acpica/dswexec.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/acpica/dswexec.c
@@ -397,11 +397,11 @@ acpi_status acpi_ds_exec_end_op(struct acpi_walk_state *walk_state)
 
 			/* Resolve all operands */
 
-			union acpi_operand_object **stack_ptr = NULL;
-			if (walk_state->num_operands > 0)
-				stack_ptr = ACPI_WALK_OPERANDS;
 			status = acpi_ex_resolve_operands(walk_state->opcode,
-							  stack_ptr,
+							  &(walk_state->
+							    operands
+							    [walk_state->
+							     num_operands - 1]),
 							  walk_state);
 		}
 
